wolfTPM v4.2.0 PC Client PCR startup values for HIRS system tests.

PCRs 17-22 start at all ones on Startup(CLEAR), before a DRTM reset. wolfTPM
v4.2.0 initializes every PCR to zero, so otherwise-valid firmware quotes fail
against the PCR digest reconstructed from the event log. This changes only initialization on 
Startup(CLEAR) and keeps the existing PCR_Reset behavior.
Remove this patch once the pinned upstream release supports these defaults.

See the following:
https://trustedcomputinggroup.org/wp-content/uploads/PC-Client-Specific-Platform-TPM-Profile-for-TPM-2p0-v1p07_Pub.pdf

--- a/src/fwtpm/fwtpm_command.c
+++ b/src/fwtpm/fwtpm_command.c
@@ -830,7 +830,10 @@
             }
             for (b = 0; b < FWTPM_PCR_BANKS; b++) {
                 for (i = 0; i < IMPLEMENTATION_PCR; i++) {
-                    XMEMSET(ctx->pcrDigest[i][b], 0, TPM_MAX_DIGEST_SIZE);
+                    /* PC Client DRTM PCRs start at all ones until a
+                     * DRTM reset; the other PCRs start at zero. */
+                    XMEMSET(ctx->pcrDigest[i][b],
+                        (i >= 17 && i <= 22) ? 0xFF : 0, TPM_MAX_DIGEST_SIZE);
                 }
             }
             ctx->globalNvWriteLock = 0;
